With [Office in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/microsoft-copilot-blog/office-at-ignite-2026-from-apps-to-agentic-system-of-work/4572226), you can go the other way. Start with a request in chat, then click into the Word document it opens alongside the conversation and edit it yourself. I find that reversal more interesting than the position of either pane. You can begin talking through what you need while the document is still taking shape.

## Speech and sketches in the same workspace

In [SketchGPT](https://zaynehuang.github.io/SketchGPT/), a prototype presented at UIST 2025, you can draw directly over an app while speaking. In the paper’s travel example, someone traces the route they have in mind and sketches a table for the itinerary. They explain aloud what should go in it. The system turns the request into a list of proposed actions for the person to check before it takes them.

