## A pizza crawl that starts with a sentence

Here’s one way I can imagine this working. I open a blank page with a place to type and a microphone. I say, “Show me the five nearest pizza places.” A map appears on the page. There’s a small gear on the map, and opening it gives me a few styles I can pick from. Light, dark, terrain. I can see which one makes the streets easiest to read.

The same controls give me a place to ask for something more specific. “What’s the shortest walking route that takes in all five?” A line appears on the map and I can see the order it picked. I could just as easily have asked how far apart the places are on average.

Then I click beneath the map and type “My pizza crawl” and a note about where to meet. I ask to make the page into a flyer and share it with Tim. When he opens the link, he can change the meeting time himself. The map can still be edited from the flyer if we decide to skip a stop.

I can imagine an interface taking shape this way. It starts with something I can say in a sentence, and the things we add to the page bring along the controls we need. I get to decide what I’m making partway through making it.

